WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.860
The Fall of the Cowboy was published
in Harper's Monthly in 1895,

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.550
to illustrate Owen Wister's essay
on the cowboy.

3
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.740
That's two years after Frederick
Jackson Turner's famous Frontier Thesis

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.340
announced that the frontier was closed.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.760
In a gray winter landscape,

6
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.510
one cowboy has climbed down
to open a gate in a wire fence,

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.550
while another waits on his horse.

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.950
Fences mean private property.

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.630
The open range is ending,
and Remington is mourning it.

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.130
The irony is that the frontier
he mourned was already a myth.
